41
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,000
But again, there's a simple answer.

42
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:51,960
If you're worried about that, don't sign.

43
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,660
Right? And this, of course, gives an incentive

44
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:57,920
to moderate the contractual punishment down to the level

45
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:58,980
people feel comfortable with.

46
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,800
But still, that's probably a very large amount.

47
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,680
Right? And enough to go and solve a lot

48
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,020
of these moral hazard problems that we see.

49
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,400
So, I mean, right now, if, say, you sign a life insurance

50
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,840
contract that says that you don't,

51
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,460
and you get the rate for a non-smoker,

52
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,680
if you die of lung cancer,

53
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:18,680
then probably there will be an investigation.

54
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:23,300
And you will, and that's, they'll say, well, wait,

55
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,860
did he work in an asbestos factory?

56
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:27,620
No. Then he was almost certainly a smoker,

57
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:28,340
and we're going to prove it.

58
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:33,220
Right? But even if they prove you were a smoker,

59
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:34,700
the worst that's likely to happen is

60
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:36,340
that they don't pay the insurance policy.

61
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:38,780
But with a contractual punishment,

62
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:41,600
actually your estate could owe the insurance company money

63
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:42,380
because you lied.

64
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:47,900
Right? And if you're willing to sign a contract like this,

65
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,940
this is a way that you could get a better rate

66
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:50,760
than you currently get.

67
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:53,040
There are, you know, so, again, there's all kinds of things

68
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,160
that you can do to endanger your life.

69
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,480
Right now, for like health or life insurance, if you were

70
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:59,420
to say, look, if I am ever caught doing any

71
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:02,560
of the following things, not only do you not have to pay me,

72
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,200
but my estate owes you money.

73
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:08,860
And, of course, contractually you'd say, and you are,

