00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:12,020
and in my, this supersedes any other will that I make,

75
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:14,580
and the insurance company must be compensated first

76
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,280
for my dishonesty.

77
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,660
Right? And this would be a way, of course, to get,

78
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:20,940
and why would anyone sign the contract?

79
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:23,500
To get lower rates, to get better coverage.

80
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,780
Right? And this way you could get around a wide range

81
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:29,820
of moral hazard problems that right now we just feel

82
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:30,500
like we have to live with.

83
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,860
Now, another interesting thing about moral hazards.

84
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:37,000
So, you possibly, I guess you're about old enough

85
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,480
to remember the Obamacare debate.

86
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,900
Now, during the Obamacare debate,

87
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:45,420
you might remember a bunch of supportive economists saying,

88
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,640
look, you can't really have a free market insurance

